# Force these to win over the flat HTML files Nitro also prerenders at the
# same paths (routeRules redirects still get prerendered as real files,
# since `routeRules: '/**': { prerender: true }` covers everything — without
# `!`, Netlify serves the existing static file instead of applying the
# redirect). See nuxt.config.ts's `/articles/*` routeRules for the source of
# truth on where each of these actually goes.
/articles/hello-world-20211126 /writing/hello-world-20211126 301!
/articles/layout-paragraphs-module-20220301 /writing/layout-paragraphs-module-20220301 301!
/articles/what-no-images-20220315 /writing/what-no-images-20220315 301!
/articles/decoupling-configuration-config-pages-20220412 /writing/decoupling-configuration-config-pages-20220412 301!

# The feed aliases do not currently need the `!` — checked the build output,
# and Nitro emits no dist/feed.xml or dist/rss.xml stub, apparently because it
# skips prerendering routes that carry a file extension. Forced anyway: the
# routes above prove this repo has already shipped that exact bug once, and
# nothing in the config stops a future change (a link in <head>, an entry in
# nitro.prerender.routes) from making these prerender too. Costs nothing while
# the stub is absent.
/feed.xml /blog.xml 301!
/rss.xml /blog.xml 301!
